/*
 * t_v40.c -- host tests for the /dev/vcu device model (gpu/hwcodec/vcu/n2vcu.c).
 *
 * Oracle, as the work package requires:
 *   - every guest struct is built field by field at a literal offset (put32/put64/put_bytes),
 *     never by assigning a C struct, so a layout mistake in mtk_vcu_abi.h cannot cancel out;
 *   - the sizes/offsets/request numbers are cross-checked three ways: the armv7a probe of the
 *     *kernel* header (layout_probe.c -> probe_values.h, generated by run_tests.sh), the same
 *     numbers in mtk_vcu_abi.h, and literals here;
 *   - expectations come from reading mtk_vcu.c / mtk_vcodec_mem.c (line cited per test);
 *   - two back ends: a recording fake in this file (exact rwvc_reg_op sequences, DMA and IRQ
 *     scripting) and T02's tests/hw/n2vc_hw_fake.c through the frozen n2vc_hw_open_fake().
 *
 * The n2vc_dma_* functions of include/n2vc_hw.h are implemented at the bottom of this file as a
 * test stand-in for V41's ap/n2vc_dma.c (guest shadow per handle, sync through hw->dma_rw).
 */
